  abstract  = {In this paper, we present a fully integrated receiver for NMR microscopy applications realized in a 0.13 micrometer CMOS technology. The chip co-integrates a planar detection coil together with a complete low-IF downconversion receiver consisting of a low noise amplifier, a quadrature downconversion mixer, a baseband amplifier stage and line drivers. The chip operates from a single 1.5V supply and consumes about 12 mA of current. The active chip area is about 350 by 450 square micrometers. The detector's measured input referred voltage noise density at the operating frequency of 300 MHz is 260 picovolt per root hertz resulting in a measured spin sensitivity of 2E13 spins per root hertz. Preliminary imaging experiments demonstrate the chip's capability of recording micron resolution MR images in imaging times which significantly advance the state-of-the-art.},
