  abstract  = {Although there are several books and review articles dealing with NMR of paramagnetic systems, we felt it timely to collect all NMR consequences of the metal magnetic susceptibility under a unified description. The approach is a modest attempt at giving some theoretical basis to appreciate the phenomena better, but is mainly focused on the various functional forms of these interactions. The aim is to provide the reader with an understanding of the computational context under which each functional form is better used to extract structural information from the system. A few selected examples of applications will be also given. Finally, we underline that all equations use SI units. It is important to recall that the conversion factor of magnetic susceptibility values from c.g.s. emu to SI contains 4&pi;, and this is still a source of mistakes in the NMR literature},
