  url       = {http://dx.doi.org/10.1063/1.1725040},
  abstract  = {The changes in the electric field gradient tensor q induced by an applied electric field E and stress del are described by the relation e(deltaq)ij = RkijsigmaEk+Tijlmsigmalm. The magnitudes and absolute signs of the five independent components of Rsigma for 35Cl in NaClO3 were measured at 77K and related to the absolute atomic configuration of the crystal. The numerical values are in units of 109 cm-1, R111sigma = -0.42, R222sigma = -2.43, R333sigma = -2.22, R113sigma = -1.53, and R123sigma = +3.53, with respect to the following coordinate system at a Cl site. The positive x3 axis points from Na+ to ClO3-, i.e., towards the [111] direction that develops a positive piezoelectric charge for a tension sigma33. The positive x1 axis passes through an oxygen site and x2 completes the right-handed set in the plane of the oxygen triangle. The electric field effects at constant stress and at constant strain are nearly equal. They are attributed to variations in the electron orbitals of the chlorate group and to changes in the ionic lattice sums outside this group.},
  comment   = {Suggested filename = Collins1964jun Stark effects on the nuclear quadrupole coupling of 35Cl in sodium chlorate 10.1063/1.1725040 *.pdf},
  file      = {Collins1964jun Stark effects on the nuclear quadrupole coupling of 35Cl in sodium chlorate 10.1063\:1.1725040 *.pdf:UNSORTED/Collins1964jun Stark effects on the nuclear quadrupole coupling of 35Cl in sodium chlorate 10.1063\:1.1725040 *.pdf:PDF},
  keywords  = {Stark effect, magnetic resonance > Stark shifts},
