  url       = {http://dx.doi.org/10.1116/1.4867753},
  abstract  = {A method of patterning magnetic metallic thin films is presented using a bilayer polymethyl methacrylate and hydrogen silsesquioxane electron beam lithography resist mask combined with ion beam etching. The bilayer resist process allows for the combination of a high-resolution resist mask with easy postprocess removal of the mask without damage to the magnetic quality of the film. Co60Fe20B20 and Co/Ni multilayer films were patterned with electron beam lithography at 10--125~keV down to 25~nm wide features with 2~nm average root-mean square edge roughness. Both the in-plane and out-of-plane magnetic anisotropies of the respective film types were preserved after patterning.},
