  url       = {http://dx.doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.7.9},
  abstract  = {The Br<sup>81</sup> quadrupole resonance in a single crystal of NaBrO<sub>3</sub> was found to be shifted and distorted by the application of electric fields of about 10 kV cm<sup>-1</sup>. This was consistent with a frequency shift proportional to the applied field, for each of the non-equivalent ions in the unit cell. Such shifts, caused by changes in the electric field gradients at the nuclei, are only expected where, as here, there is no inversion symmetry about the nuclear sites. The piezoelectric contribution to the shift was estimated to be less than 10% of the whole. },
