John Marohn earned a B.S. in Chemistry and a B.A. in Physics from the University of Rochester, earned a Ph.D. in Chemistry working with Daniel P. Weitekamp at the California Institute of Technology, and did postdoctoral work at the U.S. Army Research Laboratory as a U.S. National Research Council Postdoctoral Associate. He joined the Cornell faculty in 1999 where he is a member of the Cornell Center for Materials Research and a member of the Field of Materials Science and Engineering. In 2006, Marohn created the first international conference on nanometer-scale magnetic resonance imaging; the 5th International nano-MRI conference was held in 2015. In AY 2011 he was a visiting scientist at The Scripps Research Institute in La Jolla, California.},
