  abstract  = {We describe a novel spin polarization transfer phenomenon observed in high-field, optically pumped NMR experiments on single-crystal indium phosphide. Polarization transfer from 115In spins to 31P spins occurs when a weak radio-frequency field is applied at the 31P NMR frequency. Unlike other known high-field polarization transfer effects, no rf field near the 115In frequency is required. We present evidence that the 31P polarization arises from a state of optically pumped dipolar order in the 115In spin system and propose two mechanisms that may contribute to the creation of this state.},
