  abstract  = {We use a quantum point contact (QPC) as a displacement transducer to measure and control the low-temperature thermal motion of a nearby micromechanical cantilever. The QPC is included in an active feedback loop designed to cool the cantilever's fundamental mechanical mode, achieving a squashing of the QPC noise at high gain. The minimum achieved effective mode temperature of 0.2~K and the displacement resolution of $10^{-11}$~m/$\sqrt(\mathrm{Hz})$ are limited by the performance of the QPC as a one-dimensional conductor and by the cantilever-QPC capacitive coupling.},
