  abstract  = {We report on the fabrication of N,N$^\prime$-ditridecyl-perylene-3,4:9,10-tetracarboxylic diimide--C13 (PTCDI--C13), n-channel organic thin-film transistors (OTFTs) with 30 nm Al2O3 whose surface has been un-modified or modified with hexamethyldisilazane (HMDS) and thin hydrophobic CYTOP. Among all the devices, the OTFTs with CYTOP-modified dielectrics exhibit the most superior device performance and stability. The optimum post-annealing temperature for organic n-channels on CYTOP was also found to be as low as 80 $\deg$C, although the post-annealing was previously implemented at 120--140 $\deg$C for PTCDI domain growth in general. The low temperature of 80 $\deg$C hardly damages the CYTOP/n-channel organic interface which is deformed at a temperature higher than the glass transition temperature of CYTOP (110 $\deg$C). The pentacenequinone passivation layer turned out to be helpful to keep the interfacial trap density minimum, according to the photo-excited charge collection spectroscopy results for our 80 $\deg$C-annealed OTFTs with CYTOP-modified dielectrics.},
