  abstract  = {The exciton secondary emission spectrum of CdS crystals has been studied at 2 K under lambda equals 4765 A Ar** plus laser excitation in the samples with different exciton lifetime. Under these conditions, three distinct components of secondary emission - Raman scattering, hot and equilibrium luminescence were spectrally resolved. It has been shown that the exciton lifetime acts like a very fast optical shutter and makes it possible to observe under stationary conditions the temporal evolution of the exciton secondary emission spectrum. The energy relaxation of excitons is accompanied by its &Prime;phase&Prime; relaxation, the measure of the latter being the polarization degree of emission. With the aid of the Hanle effect, the acoustic phonon relaxation time 3. 5 multiplied by 10** minus **1**2 sec has been estimated. The exciton lifetime has been found to vary from 3 multiplied by 10** minus **1**2 to 1. 6 multiplied by 10 ** minus **9 sec in the samples studied.},
