  abstract  = {A regio-regular poly(3-hexylthiophene) (RRP3HT) thin film transistor having a split gate architecture has been fabricated on a doped silicon/silicon nitride substrate and characterized. This device demonstrates AND logic functionality. The device functionality was controlled by applying either 0 or -10 V to each of the gate electrodes. When -10 V was simultaneously applied to both gates, the device was conductive (on), while any other combination of gate voltages rendered the device resistive (off). The p-type carrier charge mobility was about 5&times;10<sup>-4</sup> cm<sup>2</sup>/V s. The low mobility is attributed to the sharp contours of the RRP3HT film due to substrate nonplanarity. A significant advantage of this architecture is that AND logic devices with multiple inputs can be fabricated using a single RRP3HT channel with multiple gates},
