  url       = {http://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1002/bbpc.19740781113/abstract},
  abstract  = {Pulse sequences with pseudo-random binary amplitude or phase modulation for broad band NMR excitation are easily implemented and require less rf peak power and dynamic range in signal processing as compared to single pulse excitation. Their main disadvantage lay in the time- and core-consuming data processing. This has been remedied with the aid of the fast Hadamard transformation which effects a fast correlation of excitation and signal in the time-domain. The calculated function resembles the common PFT-FID signal and serves a s input for the fast Fourier transform. The Bloch equations are numerically solved in order to determine the effect of rf pulse height and length.},
