  abstract  = {Epitaxial assembly of quantum dots into ordered superlattices is a new and exciting route to two-dimensional materials. Theoretical models of these assemblies predict interesting electronic behavior. Actual samples however, can not yet be fabricated of a quality approaching the models. In this work we fabricate superlattices with registry of the quantum dots to within a single atomic bond length. Despite the high degree of structural symmetry, charge carriers are surprisingly strongly localized. Calculations that account for the real measured disorder however, confirm strong localization and predict complete delocalization is possible by optimizing dot-to-dot connections.},
