In our protocol, electron-spin magnetic resonance is detected mechanically: a scanned magnet-tipped cantilever is brought near the sample, modulated microwaves are applied to resonantly excite electron spins, and changes in spin magnetization are detected as a shift in the mechanical frequency of the cantilever.
By carefully applying resonant microwaves in short bursts in synchrony with the cantilever's oscillation, we propose to retain high spatial resolution even at large cantilever amplitude where sensitivity is highest.
